.TH KAGI-VOLUME-LIBVIRT-SCSI 1 "September 2026" "Kagi 0.38.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-volume-libvirt-scsi \- generate libvirt SCSI attachment configuration for a Kagi volume
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kagi-volume-libvirt-scsi
[ARGS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Produces libvirt/QEMU configuration that presents the backend as a SCSI disk, normally via virtio-scsi, with discard/unmap enabled so guest TRIM can reclaim sparse Kagi extents.
.SH SEE ALSO
kagi-volume-qemu-scsi(1), virsh(1)
